.\" DESCRIPTION chapter
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B chdman
can be used to create, convert, check the integrity of and
extract data from media images in CHD (Compressed Hunks of Data) format.
.PP
The basic usage is \f[CR]chdman <command> <option>...\f[R]
.\"
.\"
.SS Common options
.TP
The options available depend on the command, 
but the following options are used by multiple commands:
.TP
.B \(eninput  / \-i
.TP
.IP
Specify the input file. This option is required for most commands. 
The input file formats supported depend on the command
.IP
.TP
.B \(eninputparent  / \-ip
.TP
.IP
Specify the parent CHD file for the input file. 
This option is supported for most commands that operate on CHD format 
input files. This option must be used if the input file is a delta CHD, 
storing only the hunks that differ from its parent CHD.
.IP
.TP
.B \(eninputstartbyte  / \-isb
.TP
.IP
Specify the offset to the data in the input file in bytes. 
This is useful for creating CHD format files from input files 
that contain a header before the start of the data, or for extracting 
partial content from a CHD format file. May not be specified in 
combination with the \(ga\-\-inputstarthunk\(ga / \(ga\-ish\(ga option.
.IP
.TP
.B \(eninputstarthunk  / \-ish
.TP
.IP
Specify the offset to the data in the input file in hunks. 
May not be specified in combination with 
the \(ga\-\-inputstartbyte\(ga / \(ga\-isb\(ga option.
.IP
.TP
.B \(eninputbytes  / \-ib
.TP
.IP
Specify the amount of input data to use in bytes, 
starting from the offset to the data in the input file. 
This is useful for creating CHD format files from input files that 
contain additional content after the data, or for extracting 
partial content from a CHD format file. 
May not be specified in combination with 
the \(ga\-\-inputhunks\(ga / \(ga\-ih\(ga option.
.IP
.TP
.B \(eninputhunks  / \-ih
.TP
.IP
Specify the amount of input data to use in hunks, 
starting from the offset to the data in the input file. 
May not be specified in combination with 
the \(ga\-\-inputbytes\(ga / \(ga\-ib\(ga option.
.IP
.TP
.B \(enoutput  / \-o
.TP
.IP
Specify the output file name. This option is required for 
commands that produce output files. 
The output file formats supported depend on the command.
.IP
.TP
.B \(enoutputparent  / \-op
.TP
.IP
Specify the parent CHD file for the output file. 
This option is supported for commands that produce CHD format 
output files. Using this option produces a delta CHD, 
storing only the hunks that differ from its parent CHD. 
The parent CHD should be the same media type and size, 
with the same hunk size.
.IP
.TP
.B \(encompression none|[,]\&... / \-c none|[,]\&...
.TP
.IP
Specify compression algorithms to use. This option is supported for 
commands that produce CHD format output files. 
Specify none to disable compression, or specify up to 
four comma\-separated compression algorithms. 
See compression algorithms for supported compression algorithms. 
Compression must be disable to create writable media image files.
.IP
.TP
.B \(enhunksize  / \-hs
.TP
.IP
Specifies the hunk size in bytes. This option is supported for 
commands that produce CHD format output files. 
The hunk size must be no smaller than 16 bytes and no larger 
than 1048576 bytes (1 MiB). The hunk size must be a multiple 
of the sector size or unit size of the media. Larger hunk sizes 
may give better compression ratios, but reduce performance for small 
random reads as an entire hunk needs to be read and decompressed at a time.
.IP
.TP
.B \(enforce / \-f
.TP
.IP
Overwrite output files if they already exist. This option is supported 
for commands that produce output files.
.IP
.TP
.B \(enverbose / \-v
.TP
.IP
Enable verbose output. This prints more detailed information for some commands.
.IP
.TP
.B \(ennumprocessors  / \-np
.TP
.IP
Limit the maximum number of concurrent threads used for data compression. 
This option is supported for commands that produce CHD format output files.
.IP
.TP
.SS Commands
.TP
.\"
.TP
.SS info
.TP
.IP
Display information about a CHD format file.
Information includes:
.IP \(bu 2
CHD format version and compression algorithms used.
.IP \(bu 2
Compressed and uncompressed sizes and overall compression ratio.
.IP \(bu 2
Hunk size, unit size and number of hunks in the file.
.IP \(bu 2
SHA1 digests of the data and metadata.
.PP
Common options supported:
.IP \(bu 2
.B \f[CR]\-\-input <file>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-i <file>\f[R] (required)
.IP \(bu 2
.B \f[CR]\-\-verbose\f[R] / \f[CR]\-v\f[R]
.\"
.TP
.SS verify
.TP
.IP
Verify the integrity of a CHD format file.
The input file must be a read\-only CHD format file (the integrity of
writable CHD files cannot be verified). Note that this command modifies 
its input file if the \f[CR]\-\-fix\f[R] / \f[CR]\-f\f[R] option is specified.
.PP
Common options supported:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-input <file>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-i <file>\f[R] (required)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-inputparent <chdfile>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-ip <chdfile>\f[R]
.PP
Additional options:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-fix\f[R] / \f[CR]\-f\f[R]
.\"
.TP
.SS createraw
.TP
.IP
Create a CHD format file from a raw media image.
.PP
Common options supported:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-input <file>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-i <file>\f[R] (required)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-inputstartbyte <offset>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-isb <offset>\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-inputstarthunk <offset>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-ish <offset>\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-inputbytes <length>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-ib <length>\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-inputhunks <length>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-ih <length>\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-output <file>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-o <file>\f[R] (required)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-outputparent <chdfile>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-op <chdfile>\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-compression none|<type>[,<type>]...\f[R] /
\f[CR]\-c none|<type>[,<type>]...\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-hunksize <bytes>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-hs <bytes>\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-force\f[R] / \f[CR]\-f\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-numprocessors <count>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-np <count>\f[R]
.PP
Additional options:
.PP
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-unitsize <bytes>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-us <bytes>\f[R] (required)
.IP
.IP
The unit size for the output CHD file in bytes. 
This is the smallest unit of data that can be addressed within the CHD file. 
It should match the sector size or page size of the source media. 
The hunk size must be a whole multiple of the unit size. 
The unit size must be specified if no parent CHD file for the output is supplied. 
If a parent CHD file for the output is supplied, the unit size must match the 
unit size of the parent CHD file.
.IP
.PP
If the \f[CR]\-\-hunksize\f[R] or \f[CR]\-hs\f[R] option is not
supplied, the default will be:
.IP \(bu 2
The hunk size of the parent CHD file if a parent CHD file for the output
is supplied.
.IP \(bu 2
The smallest whole multiple of the unit size not larger than 4 KiB if
the unit size is not larger than 4 KiB (4096 bytes).
.IP \(bu 2
The unit size if it is larger than 4 KiB (4096 bytes).
.PP
If the \f[CR]\-\-compression\f[R] or \f[CR]\-c\f[R] option is not
supplied, it defaults to \f[CR]lzma,zlib,huff,flac\f[R].
.\"
.SS createhd
.TP
.IP
Create a CHD format hard disk image file.
.PP
Common options supported:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-input <file>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-i <file>\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-inputstartbyte <offset>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-isb <offset>\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-inputstarthunk <offset>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-ish <offset>\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-inputbytes <length>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-ib <length>\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-inputhunks <length>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-ih <length>\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-output <file>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-o <file>\f[R] (required)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-outputparent <chdfile>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-op <chdfile>\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-compression none|<type>[,<type>]...\f[R] /
\f[CR]\-c none|<type>[,<type>]...\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-hunksize <bytes>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-hs <bytes>\f[R] (required)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-force\f[R] / \f[CR]\-f\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-numprocessors <count>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-np <count>\f[R]
.PP
Additional options:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-sectorsize <bytes>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-ss <bytes>\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-size <bytes>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-s <bytes>\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-chs <cylinders>,<heads>,<sectors>\f[R] /
\f[CR]\-chs <cylinders>,<heads>,<sectors>\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-template <template>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-tp <template>\f[R]
.PP
Creates a blank (zero\-filled) hard disk image if no input file is
supplied.
The input start/length (\f[CR]\-\-inputstartbyte\f[R] / \f[CR]\-isb\f[R]
, \f[CR]\-\-inputstarthunk\f[R] / \f[CR]\-ish\f[R] ,
\f[CR]\-\-inputbytes\f[R] / \f[CR]\-ib\f[R] and
\f[CR]\-\-inputhunks\f[R] / \f[CR]\-ih\f[R] options) cannot be used if
no input file is supplied.
.PP
If the \f[CR]\-\-hunksize\f[R] or \f[CR]\-hs\f[R] option is not
supplied, the default will be:
.IP \(bu 2
The hunk size of the parent CHD file if a parent CHD file for the output
is supplied.
.IP \(bu 2
The smallest whole multiple of the sector size not larger than 4 KiB if
the sector size is not larger than 4 KiB (4096 bytes).
.IP \(bu 2
The sector size if it is larger than 4 KiB (4096 bytes).
.PP
If the \f[CR]\-\-compression\f[R] or \f[CR]\-c\f[R] option is not
supplied, it defaults to \f[CR]lzma,zlib,huff,flac\f[R] if an input file
is supplied, or \f[CR]none\f[R] if no input file is supplied.
.\"
.SS createcd
.TP
.IP
Create a CHD format CD\-ROM image file.
.PP
Common options supported:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-input <file>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-i <file>\f[R] (required)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-output <file>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-o <file>\f[R] (required)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-outputparent <chdfile>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-op <chdfile>\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-compression none|<type>[,<type>]...\f[R] /
\f[CR]\-c none|<type>[,<type>]...\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-hunksize <bytes>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-hs <bytes>\f[R] (required)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-force\f[R] / \f[CR]\-f\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-numprocessors <count>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-np <count>\f[R]
.PP
If the \f[CR]\-\-hunksize\f[R] or \f[CR]\-hs\f[R] option is not
supplied, the default will be the hunk size of the parent CHD if a
parent CHD file for the output is supplied, or eight sectors per hunk
(18,816 bytes) otherwise.
.PP
If the \f[CR]\-\-compression\f[R] or \f[CR]\-c\f[R] option is not
supplied, it defaults to \f[CR]cdlz,cdzl,cdfl\f[R].
.\"
.SS createdvd
.TP
.IP
Create a CHD format DVD\-ROM image file.
.PP
Common options supported:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-input <file>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-i <file>\f[R] (required)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-inputstartbyte <offset>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-isb <offset>\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-inputstarthunk <offset>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-ish <offset>\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-inputbytes <length>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-ib <length>\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-inputhunks <length>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-ih <length>\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-output <file>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-o <file>\f[R] (required)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-outputparent <chdfile>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-op <chdfile>\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-compression none|<type>[,<type>]...\f[R] /
\f[CR]\-c none|<type>[,<type>]...\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-hunksize <bytes>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-hs <bytes>\f[R] (required)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-force\f[R] / \f[CR]\-f\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-numprocessors <count>\f[R] / \f[CR]\-np <count>\f[R]
.PP
If the \f[CR]\-\-hunksize\f[R] or \f[CR]\-hs\f[R] option is not
supplied, the default will be the hunk size of the parent CHD if a
parent CHD file for the output is supplied, or two sectors per hunk
(4096 bytes) otherwise.
.PP
If the \f[CR]\-\-compression\f[R] or \f[CR]\-c\f[R] option is not
supplied, it defaults to \f[CR]lzma,zlib,huff,flac\f[R].
.\"
